### CertHub exploratory API calls (REST Client)
### Flow: List System Requirements / Verification / Validation content by KT
###
### Setup:
### 1. Copy IDs/URLs from certhub.toml (do not invent values here).
### 2. Set @apiKey from CERTHUB_API_KEY in .env (prod showcase tenant).
### 3. Run the three "List records" requests — confirm counts and data.name values.
### 4. Optionally Get KT (requirements) for Tech Doc metadata used by sync project info.
###
### ID mapping (dashboard URL uses history; Records context uses revision):
###   knowledgeTopicId = *_kt_history_id → context.knowledge_unit_topic_id = *_kt_id
###   Prefer: `uv run cadence config-get <field>` over hand-editing these vars.
###
### Note: put ObjectIds literally in JSON bodies — some REST Client builds leave
### {{fileVar}} unsubstituted inside JSON (e.g. {{productId}} stored as text).

# Prod showcase tenant (must match certhub.toml)
@techdocBase = https://techdoc.prod.certhub-containers.containers.certhub.tech
@recordsBase = https://records.prod.certhub-containers.containers.certhub.tech
@tracerBase = https://tracer.prod.certhub-containers.containers.certhub.tech
@apiKey = {{$dotenv CERTHUB_API_KEY}}
@reqKtId = 69b989b54252b7481003b10a
@verifKtId = 69b989b54252b7481003b110
@validKtId = 69b989b54252b7481003b112
@productHistoryId = 69b9899f4252b7481003afaa
@kuHistoryId = 69b989a14252b7481003afe5
@recordId = 000000000000000000000000

### =============================================================================
### 1. Get requirements KT (Tech Doc metadata)
### =============================================================================

# @name getKt
GET {{techdocBase}}/kt/{{reqKtId}}
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}
Accept: application/json

### =============================================================================
### 2. List records — Requirements / Verification / Validation
### =============================================================================

# @name listRequirements
GET {{recordsBase}}/records/?context__knowledge_unit_topic_id={{reqKtId}}
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}
Accept: application/json

###

# @name listVerification
GET {{recordsBase}}/records/?context__knowledge_unit_topic_id={{verifKtId}}
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}
Accept: application/json

###

# @name listValidation
GET {{recordsBase}}/records/?context__knowledge_unit_topic_id={{validKtId}}
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}
Accept: application/json

### =============================================================================
### 3. Read one record
### =============================================================================

# @name getRecord
GET {{recordsBase}}/records/{{recordId}}
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}
Accept: application/json

### =============================================================================
### 4. Create record on requirements KT
### form starts as {}; replace with a real form from List/Get if validation requires it.
### Product dashboard needs linked_product + knowledge_unit_id (KU revision), not KT alone.
### Resolve KU revision via Tech Doc GET /ku/{kuHistoryId} → id before create.
### =============================================================================

# @name createRecord
POST {{recordsBase}}/records/
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}
Accept: application/json
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Sterilization temperature range is better",
  "form": {},
  "data": {
    "name": "Sterilization temperature range is better",
    "description": "Device shall achieve and maintain sterilization temperature of 121°C ± 2°C",
    "type": "functional",
    "priority": "high",
    "source": "Functional & Performance Requirements"
  },
  "context": {
    "linked_product": "69b9899f4252b7481003afaa",
    "knowledge_unit_id": "REPLACE_WITH_KU_REVISION",
    "knowledge_unit_topic_id": "69b989b54252b7481003b10a"
  }
}

### =============================================================================
### 5. Patch context on a bad/orphan create
### Set @recordId to the row to repair, then send.
### =============================================================================

# @name patchRecordContext
PATCH {{recordsBase}}/records/{{recordId}}
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}
Accept: application/json
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "context": {
    "linked_product": "69b9899f4252b7481003afaa",
    "knowledge_unit_id": "REPLACE_WITH_KU_REVISION",
    "knowledge_unit_topic_id": "69b989b54252b7481003b10a"
  }
}

### =============================================================================
### 6. Update record data (PATCH — by-id write; OpenAPI PUT is upsert-by-linked-document)
### =============================================================================

# @name updateRecord
PATCH {{recordsBase}}/records/{{recordId}}
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}
Accept: application/json
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Sterilization temperature range is better (updated)",
  "data": {
    "name": "Sterilization temperature range is better (updated)",
    "description": "Device shall achieve and maintain sterilization temperature of 121°C ± 2°C",
    "type": "functional",
    "priority": "high",
    "source": "Functional & Performance Requirements"
  }
}

### =============================================================================
### 7. Tracer — smoke-check traces for one KT (System Requirements)
### Confirmed: GET /traces and POST /traces/batch/list work (200) with Cadence key.
### GET /traces/list and /traces/all still return 401 Invalid API key for that key.
### docs.certhub.de hosts docs only — call {{tracerBase}}, not docs.certhub.de.
### Sync joins via Record batch/list + requirements_use_case topic→topic rules.
### =============================================================================

@productVersion = 0.1

# @name tracesForRequirementsKt
GET {{tracerBase}}/traces?node_id={{reqKtId}}&node_type=KnowledgeTopic&version={{productVersion}}
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}
Accept: application/json

###

# @name batchListTraces
# Sync sends every synced Record _id this way. Demo: one SYSREQ + one VERIF + one DOUT.
# Use literal ObjectIds in JSON (REST Client may not expand {{vars}}).
POST {{tracerBase}}/traces/batch/list
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "nodes": [
    {
      "node_id": "69c2d6756406f437042965e5",
      "node_type": "Record",
      "version": ""
    },
    {
      "node_id": "69c2d6826406f437042965f4",
      "node_type": "Record",
      "version": ""
    },
    {
      "node_id": "69c2d67f6406f437042965ef",
      "node_type": "Record",
      "version": ""
    }
  ],
  "n_hops": 1,
  "mode": "legacy_connected_nodes"
}